The cancer is an infiltrating ductal carcinoma of the right breast, with focal lobular features, and the primary site is the right breast; 
The tumor measures 4 x 6 x 7 cm; 
The histologic differentiation grade is 2 (Elston SBR grade; A/N/M = 3/2/1), with a mitotic index of 4 mitoses/10 HPFs; 
There is evidence of invasion into lymphatics in the nipple, but no evidence of invasion into adjacent tissues or organs; 
There are features of lymphovascular invasion (LVI) in the nipple, but no features of perineural invasion (PNI) are described; 
The surgical margins, including the deep margin and skin over tumor, are negative for malignancy; 
A total of 11 lymph nodes were examined, including 2 sentinel nodes, and 3 are positive for metastasis; 
There is no extracapsular extension in lymph node metastases; 
There is no evidence of distant metastasis; 
The pathological AJCC stage is pT3 pN1a; 
Relevant immunohistochemistry or biomarker results are not reported in this pathology report, but it is mentioned to "see previous biopsy" for prognostic markers; 
No molecular test results are reported; 
Mitotic activity is described with a mitotic index of 4 mitoses/10 HPFs; 
There is no mention of treatment effect, regression score, or therapy response; 
Additional findings include focal benign calcification in the left breast tissue, and the right breast resection specimen shows a deep central tumor with a portion resected prior to examination, probably for research purposes.

